---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
import about from "../assets/images/about.jpg";

const updated = "28 August 2026";
---
<Base title="Terms of Service — Clear Touch Tourism & Services"
      description="Booking terms, payment, cancellation and conduct policy for Clear Touch Tourism & Services tours, transfers, photography and videography in Qatar."
      >
  <Header />

  <PageHero image={about} eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Terms of Service"
    subtitle="The terms that apply when you book a tour, transfer or shoot with Clear Touch." />

  <section class="section section--cream">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="legal prose">
        <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

        <p>
          These terms govern bookings made with {site.fullName} (&ldquo;Clear Touch&rdquo;,
          &ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;), a licensed tour operator and creative studio in {site.location},
          through <strong>cleartouchtourism.com</strong>, WhatsApp, email, our
          online scheduling tool, or in person. By confirming a booking you accept these terms.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Bookings and confirmation</h2>
        <p>
          A booking is confirmed only once we have sent you a written confirmation by email or
          WhatsApp stating the service, date, time and price. An enquiry, a quote, or a slot held in
          our scheduling tool is not itself a confirmed booking. Please check your confirmation
          carefully and tell us straight away if any detail is wrong.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Prices and payment</h2>
        <p>
          Prices are quoted per booking and depend on the group size, season and inclusions. Unless
          stated otherwise, prices are in Qatari Riyal (QAR) and include the items listed under
          &ldquo;What&rsquo;s included&rdquo; for that service. Anything listed under
          &ldquo;Not included&rdquo; — entry tickets, meals, optional activities, gratuities and
          personal expenses — is payable by you.
        </p>
        <p>
          A deposit may be required to secure a date, with the balance due before or on the day of
          service as set out in your confirmation. We will tell you the exact amount and payment
          method in writing before you pay anything.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Changes and cancellation by you</h2>
        <p>
          Tell us as early as you can if your plans change and we will do our best to move your
          booking. The cancellation terms that apply to your booking are stated in your written
          confirmation, because they differ between services — a desert safari, a resort island day
          pass and a full photography shoot each carry different commitments to third parties. Where
          we have already paid a resort, boat operator or venue on your behalf, that portion may be
          non-refundable.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Changes and cancellation by us</h2>
        <p>
          Safety comes first. We may change or cancel a tour because of weather, sea conditions, desert
          or road conditions, vehicle or vessel issues, government restrictions, or anything else
          outside our reasonable control. Where that happens we will offer you the first of these that
          works for you: a rescheduled date, a comparable alternative experience, or a refund of the
          amount you paid for the affected part.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Your responsibilities</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Be at the agreed pickup point at the agreed time. Where a group departure is missed, it may not be possible to refund or repeat it.</li>
          <li>Carry valid identification, and any visa or permit your itinerary requires.</li>
          <li>Tell us in advance about medical conditions, pregnancy, mobility needs, allergies or dietary requirements that affect the activity.</li>
          <li>Follow the reasonable safety instructions of your guide, driver or skipper at all times.</li>
          <li>Supervise children in your party. Minors must be accompanied by a parent or guardian.</li>
          <li>Respect Qatari law and local custom, including dress and conduct at cultural and religious sites.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We may end a service without refund if a guest&rsquo;s behaviour puts themselves, other
          guests or our team at risk.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Activity risk</h2>
        <p>
          Some of our experiences — dune bashing, camel riding, sandboarding, water sports and boat
          travel — carry inherent risk even when properly conducted. You take part voluntarily and
          accept that risk. Please do not join an activity that is unsuitable for your health.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Insurance</h2>
        <p>
          We are licensed and insured as an operator. That cover does not replace personal travel
          insurance, and we strongly recommend you hold your own policy covering medical costs,
          cancellation and personal belongings.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Visa assistance</h2>
        <p>
          Where we help with a Qatar tourist visa, we prepare and submit the application on your
          behalf. The decision belongs entirely to the Qatari authorities. We cannot guarantee an
          outcome, and service fees for work already done are not refundable if an application is
          refused.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Photography and video services</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Delivery.</strong> Edited images and films are delivered digitally within the timeframe stated in your booking confirmation.</li>
          <li><strong>Copyright.</strong> We retain copyright in the images and footage we create. You receive a licence to use your delivered files for personal use, or for the commercial use agreed in writing for a commercial commission.</li>
          <li><strong>Portfolio use.</strong> We may wish to show selected work in our portfolio or on social media. We will ask you first, and we will respect a no.</li>
          <li><strong>Raw files.</strong> Unedited raw files are not part of a standard delivery.</li>
          <li><strong>Creative judgement.</strong> Editing style is our professional judgement, in the style shown in our portfolio. Re-edits beyond the agreed revisions may be chargeable.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>10. Website content</h2>
        <p>
          All photographs, video, text and design on this website belong to {site.fullName} and may not
          be copied or reused without our written permission. We keep this site as accurate as we can,
          but itineraries, timings and inclusions can change; your written booking confirmation is what
          governs your booking.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Liability</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing in these terms limits liability for death or personal injury caused by our
          negligence, or for anything else that cannot be limited under Qatari law. Beyond that, our
          liability for any booking is limited to the amount you paid us for it, and we are not liable
          for indirect losses such as missed flights or onward arrangements.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Complaints</h2>
        <p>
          If something goes wrong, tell your guide at the time so we have the chance to put it right on
          the spot. If it is still unresolved, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> within 30 days and
          we will respond.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Qatar, and the courts of Qatar have
          jurisdiction over any dispute.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          {site.fullName}<br />
          {site.location}<br />
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a><br />
          <a href={`tel:${site.phoneRaw}`}>{site.phone}</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .legal { max-width: 780px; }
  .legal__updated { font-size: .9rem; color: var(--teal); font-weight: 600; }
  .legal h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.4rem; color: var(--ink);
    margin: 38px 0 14px;
  }
  .legal ul { margin-top: 16px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }
  .legal li { color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.7; padding-left: 18px; position: relative; }
  .legal li::before {
    content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; top: .65em;
    width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--gold);
  }
  .legal a { color: var(--gold-dark); text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
